  "findings": [
    "The networks are the 1.6.1 networks with `cell` renamed to `sample` (`cell_encoder`->`sample_encoder`, `cell_bias`->`sample_bias`). Layer creation order is unchanged, so the seeded initialization and the dropout draws coincide; the checkpoint of a 1.6.1 net loads after renaming those two prefixes.",
    "v2 featurizes inside the pipeline: `scaledGeneExpression(transform=rank)` fits the sorted training-sample reference and the scaler on the unique training samples (as 1.6.1 does) and returns float32; 1.6.1 casts to float32 after scaling in float64. The rank transform itself is compared before the scaler and is exact.",
    "v2 builds the drug id-embedding table over the drugs of the training and early-stopping pairs, 1.6.1 over every drug with features. The case uses only drugs that occur in those pairs, so the table shapes (and with them the seeded initialization) coincide.",
    "1.6.1 returns the training mean for a pair whose sample or drug has no features; v2 returns NaN there (the pipeline's missing-feature rule) and no longer stores the training mean.",
    "Without an early-stopping set 1.6.1 holds out 10% of the pairs with the global torch RNG; v2 uses a `torch.Generator` seeded from `seed`. The case passes an explicit early-stopping set, which is the path where the two are comparable.",
    "A `n_bits` hyperparameter on the `fingerprints` featurizer applies only when the fingerprints are computed from SMILES; a precomputed `morgan_fingerprint` view is used as is (as in this case)."
  ],
